.TH QFW-DEACTIVATE 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-deactivate \- restore the shell environment saved by qfw-activate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-deactivate
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-deactivate
is a shell function defined by sourcing
.BR qfw-activate (1).
It restores the prior QFw, DEFw, Python, library, manual, and prompt settings,
then removes QFw's activation helpers from the shell.
.PP
When
.BR qfw-activate (1)
was called with
.BR --venv ,
deactivation also deactivates that virtual environment. A virtual environment
that was active before QFw activation is restored.
.PP
Deactivation does not stop services and does not remove an application run
directory. Call
.BR qfw-teardown (1)
for every prepared application runtime before deactivating QFw. Site-owned
services are stopped separately with the role command or service manager that
started them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates that the saved environment was restored.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-activate (1),
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-teardown (1),
.BR qfw (7)
